    "fixedDatesAndSyntheticKeys": true,
    "syntheticTypedArchiveChecks": "355 deterministic rows per architecture/delivered app source variant. Each save captures exact raw archive bytes/length and number of real UserDefaults.set invocations. Accounts and limits are synthetic. Cases include old entries without owner or headline, repeated IDs, placeholder glyph, UTF-16/canonical strings, signed zero, mixed numeric extrema, unencodable non-finite values, state recovery, owner lookup by snapshot identifier, full replacements, forgotten or damaged defaults, and externally removed data.",
    "storeRowsPerArch": 14,
    "actualStoreCases": "Detached public sources with synthetic providers only, actual NotchUsageStore init/refresh/invalidateAccount/signOut/failure paths, and separate real UserDefaults suites. Controlled overlapping provider responses proved partial writes and cancellation of an outdated owner. A second store overwrote the same suite; sign-out observed its contents and subsequent refresh restored the store map. Existing strictly verified owner handling differs in four observed public rows and matches c12ff160 on both architectures. No actual credential stores or external providers were accessed.",
